  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community for this meme is individuals who are familiar with or sympathetic to racist and misogynistic tropes, particularly those who endorse or find humor in violent, degrading stereotypes against Black people and Black women. The meme is designed to provoke shock and contempt by leveraging the Obamas' public status and racial identity, appealing to an audience that finds offensive, vulgar, and violent imagery amusing or acceptable. This audience likely includes people who hold or are exposed to anti-Black stereotypes (e.g., aggressive/violent nature, hypersexualization, athletic ability as sole competency) and misogynistic tropes (e.g., objectification/body part focus, emotional instability claims, gold digger accusations, crazy/hysterical labeling, age/appearance-based value judgments, maternal role limitations, sexual availability assumptions, intelligence/competence denial). The meme's crude, violent question is intended to resonate with those who view the Obamas as 'easy targets' or 'deserving' of such an attack, reinforcing existing prejudices. The audience may also include those who enjoy or are drawn to internet memes that are intentionally offensive, hateful, and shock-based, often found in online communities that prioritize edginess over sensitivity.",
